{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XqDXiScXvhGaqp4Na6uxiv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GdobHcVcqGQon44cqpBPfF","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept).\n\nYour focus areas: **Methods** and **Experiments**.\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"Circular Evaluation as Systematic Risk in Weak Supervision for Sequential Agent Data\"\n8 pages, anonymous, dated May 14 2026.\n\nThe paper studies progress stagnation detection in LLM coding agents using weak supervision (labeling functions). The core finding: standard LF-derived evaluation massively overstates detector performance due to \"circular evaluation\"—training and evaluating on labels derived from features that overlap with classifier inputs. They construct a 650-window human-annotated gold set and show:\n\n1. **Inflation**: Structural classifiers drop from F1=0.995 to 0.74-0.76 on gold (25.5pp inflation); probes drop 15.5pp; LLM-as-judge *improves* by 6.8pp on gold.\n2. **Hierarchy collapse**: Structural-over-probe gap reverses from +9pp to -1pp; structural-over-LLM collapses from +24.3pp to +3pp. All methods converge to 0.73-0.77 band.\n3. **Temporal dynamics validated**: LF temporal roles (cmd_rep leading, outcome_bp lagging) preserved on gold (KW p=0.003).\n4. **Temporal label models fail**: TWV, HMM, lag-aware HMM all fail to beat majority vote.\n\nContributions claimed: (1) first quantification of circular eval inflation in weak supervision for sequential agent data (mean 21.5pp); (2) 650-window gold benchmark with IAA κ=0.72; (3) temporal dynamics are genuine but agent-specific; (4) negative result on temporal label models.\n\n## Key Tables (from paper)\n- Table 1: Gold set stats: N=650, agreement=86%, κ=0.72, stagnation prevalence=42% (vs LF 28%)\n- Table 2: LF-Human confusion matrix: agreement=68%, κ=0.34, asymmetry ratio 1.93\n- Table 3: Per-LF agreement: cmd_rep 61%, file_diff 78%, outcome_bp 63%\n- Table 4: Inflation table: Structural RF 0.995→0.74 (-25.5pp), Probe 0.906→0.75 (-15.5pp), LLM 0.663→0.73 (+6.8pp), mean -21.5pp\n- Table 5: Gap collapse: Structural-Probe +9→-1pp (reversed), Structural-LLM +24.3→+3pp (-88%)\n- Table 6: Structural on gold: LR 0.71, RF 0.74, GB 0.76 (per-class: GB stag 0.71, prog 0.81)\n- Table 7: Probes on gold: Qwen3 0.75, E5 0.76, BGE 0.77\n- Table 8: Cross-agent (OpenHands): RF 0.68, GB 0.72, Probe-FT 0.70, inflation 23-25pp\n- Table 9: F1_stag breakdown: overall 0.86→0.70, LF-disagrees-with-gold subset 0.41\n- Table 10: Error analysis: RF 169 errors, Probe 163, LLM 176, all-3 overlap 89 (14%)\n- Table 11: Temporal dynamics: cmd_rep -1.87→-0.8, file_diff -1.2→-1.5, outcome_bp +6.7→+4.2, p=0.003\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (imagined experiments list)\nThe full experiment plan included these experiments:\n1. Gold Set — LF-Human Agreement (650 windows, confusion matrix, per-LF agreement)\n2. Gold Set — Structural RF/GB Evaluation (30-dim features on gold, inflation quantification, feature importance shift)\n3. Gold Set — Probe Evaluation (GRU probe on gold, structural-probe gap reversal)\n4. Gold Set — LLM-as-Judge Re-evaluation (Claude Sonnet on gold, deflation analysis)\n5. Gold Set — Cross-Agent Structural on Gold (OH gold subset)\n6. Gold Set — Circular Eval Inflation Quantification (comprehensive inflation/deflation summary)\n7. Gold Set — Inter-Annotator Agreement & Annotation Quality (IAA, adjudication rate)\n8. Gold Set — Error Pattern Re-analysis (error overlap, unique errors, Venn diagram)\n9. F1-Stag Per-Class Breakdown (per-class analysis on LF vs gold, by trajectory length, position, lf_agreement)\n10. Gold Set — Temporal Dynamics Validation (lag analysis on gold)\n11. Gold Set — Paper Reframe Impact Analysis (meta: claim restructuring)\n\nThe paper appears to cover experiments 1-10 substantively. Experiment 11 is meta-analysis.\n\nNotable from the experiment plan:\n- Feature importance shift analysis (cmd_rep_ratio rank 1→3, file_diff_freq rank 3→1) is mentioned in text but no dedicated table\n- Figures described in the plan (Sankey diagram, heatmaps, scatter plots, Venn diagram, dumbbell plot) are NOT present in the paper — the paper has NO figures at all\n- The plan mentions Structural LR baseline; paper includes it in Table 4 and Table 6\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate the following dimensions thoroughly:\n\n### 1. Methodological Soundness\n- Is the experimental design rigorous? Are there confounds?\n- Is the gold set construction (650 windows, 2 annotators, adjudication) adequate?\n- Are the statistical claims supported? (e.g., KW p=0.003, inflation quantification)\n- Is the \"circular evaluation\" mechanism properly formalized or just described informally?\n- Are the baselines appropriate and fairly evaluated?\n\n### 2. Experimental Completeness\n- Which planned experiments are covered vs missing?\n- Are results presented with sufficient detail (confidence intervals, significance tests)?\n- Is the cross-agent evaluation sufficient for generalization claims?\n- Are ablations adequate?\n\n### 3. Reproducibility\n- Are details sufficient to reproduce? (window size k, train/test split, hyperparameters, prompts for LLM-as-judge)\n- Is the gold set described well enough?\n\n### 4. Weaknesses in Methods/Experiments\n- What are the most serious methodological gaps?\n- What experiments would strengthen the paper?\n\nOutput your review in this format:\n\n```\n## R1 Review: Methods & Experiments\n\n### Summary\n[2-3 sentences]\n\n### Strengths\n[Bulleted list, 4-6 items]\n\n### Weaknesses\n[Bulleted list, 4-8 items, each with severity: Major/Minor]\n\n### Missing Experiments or Analysis\n[What's absent that should be present]\n\n### Questions for Authors\n[3-5 specific questions]\n\n### Detailed Comments\n[Paragraph-form deeper analysis]\n\n### Preliminary Score: X/6\n### Preliminary Confidence: X/5\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31144,"cache_read_input_tokens":22911,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31144},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afaa0581-5224-4e41-930b-491fc2855128","uuid":"9fe7fd00-31be-4e5a-8d81-ff9e812a9e8e"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a67b5442dda3709cd","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GdobHcVcqGQon44cqpBPfF","description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept).\n\nYour focus areas: **Methods** and **Experiments**.\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"Circular Evaluation as Systematic Risk in Weak Supervision for Sequential Agent Data\"\n8 pages, anonymous, dated May 14 2026.\n\nThe paper studies progress stagnation detection in LLM coding agents using weak supervision (labeling functions). The core finding: standard LF-derived evaluation massively overstates detector performance due to \"circular evaluation\"—training and evaluating on labels derived from features that overlap with classifier inputs. They construct a 650-window human-annotated gold set and show:\n\n1. **Inflation**: Structural classifiers drop from F1=0.995 to 0.74-0.76 on gold (25.5pp inflation); probes drop 15.5pp; LLM-as-judge *improves* by 6.8pp on gold.\n2. **Hierarchy collapse**: Structural-over-probe gap reverses from +9pp to -1pp; structural-over-LLM collapses from +24.3pp to +3pp. All methods converge to 0.73-0.77 band.\n3. **Temporal dynamics validated**: LF temporal roles (cmd_rep leading, outcome_bp lagging) preserved on gold (KW p=0.003).\n4. **Temporal label models fail**: TWV, HMM, lag-aware HMM all fail to beat majority vote.\n\nContributions claimed: (1) first quantification of circular eval inflation in weak supervision for sequential agent data (mean 21.5pp); (2) 650-window gold benchmark with IAA κ=0.72; (3) temporal dynamics are genuine but agent-specific; (4) negative result on temporal label models.\n\n## Key Tables (from paper)\n- Table 1: Gold set stats: N=650, agreement=86%, κ=0.72, stagnation prevalence=42% (vs LF 28%)\n- Table 2: LF-Human confusion matrix: agreement=68%, κ=0.34, asymmetry ratio 1.93\n- Table 3: Per-LF agreement: cmd_rep 61%, file_diff 78%, outcome_bp 63%\n- Table 4: Inflation table: Structural RF 0.995→0.74 (-25.5pp), Probe 0.906→0.75 (-15.5pp), LLM 0.663→0.73 (+6.8pp), mean -21.5pp\n- Table 5: Gap collapse: Structural-Probe +9→-1pp (reversed), Structural-LLM +24.3→+3pp (-88%)\n- Table 6: Structural on gold: LR 0.71, RF 0.74, GB 0.76 (per-class: GB stag 0.71, prog 0.81)\n- Table 7: Probes on gold: Qwen3 0.75, E5 0.76, BGE 0.77\n- Table 8: Cross-agent (OpenHands): RF 0.68, GB 0.72, Probe-FT 0.70, inflation 23-25pp\n- Table 9: F1_stag breakdown: overall 0.86→0.70, LF-disagrees-with-gold subset 0.41\n- Table 10: Error analysis: RF 169 errors, Probe 163, LLM 176, all-3 overlap 89 (14%)\n- Table 11: Temporal dynamics: cmd_rep -1.87→-0.8, file_diff -1.2→-1.5, outcome_bp +6.7→+4.2, p=0.003\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (imagined experiments list)\nThe full experiment plan included these experiments:\n1. Gold Set — LF-Human Agreement (650 windows, confusion matrix, per-LF agreement)\n2. Gold Set — Structural RF/GB Evaluation (30-dim features on gold, inflation quantification, feature importance shift)\n3. Gold Set — Probe Evaluation (GRU probe on gold, structural-probe gap reversal)\n4. Gold Set — LLM-as-Judge Re-evaluation (Claude Sonnet on gold, deflation analysis)\n5. Gold Set — Cross-Agent Structural on Gold (OH gold subset)\n6. Gold Set — Circular Eval Inflation Quantification (comprehensive inflation/deflation summary)\n7. Gold Set — Inter-Annotator Agreement & Annotation Quality (IAA, adjudication rate)\n8. Gold Set — Error Pattern Re-analysis (error overlap, unique errors, Venn diagram)\n9. F1-Stag Per-Class Breakdown (per-class analysis on LF vs gold, by trajectory length, position, lf_agreement)\n10. Gold Set — Temporal Dynamics Validation (lag analysis on gold)\n11. Gold Set — Paper Reframe Impact Analysis (meta: claim restructuring)\n\nThe paper appears to cover experiments 1-10 substantively. Experiment 11 is meta-analysis.\n\nNotable from the experiment plan:\n- Feature importance shift analysis (cmd_rep_ratio rank 1→3, file_diff_freq rank 3→1) is mentioned in text but no dedicated table\n- Figures described in the plan (Sankey diagram, heatmaps, scatter plots, Venn diagram, dumbbell plot) are NOT present in the paper — the paper has NO figures at all\n- The plan mentions Structural LR baseline; paper includes it in Table 4 and Table 6\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate the following dimensions thoroughly:\n\n### 1. Methodological Soundness\n- Is the experimental design rigorous? Are there confounds?\n- Is the gold set construction (650 windows, 2 annotators, adjudication) adequate?\n- Are the statistical claims supported? (e.g., KW p=0.003, inflation quantification)\n- Is the \"circular evaluation\" mechanism properly formalized or just described informally?\n- Are the baselines appropriate and fairly evaluated?\n\n### 2. Experimental Completeness\n- Which planned experiments are covered vs missing?\n- Are results presented with sufficient detail (confidence intervals, significance tests)?\n- Is the cross-agent evaluation sufficient for generalization claims?\n- Are ablations adequate?\n\n### 3. Reproducibility\n- Are details sufficient to reproduce? (window size k, train/test split, hyperparameters, prompts for LLM-as-judge)\n- Is the gold set described well enough?\n\n### 4. Weaknesses in Methods/Experiments\n- What are the most serious methodological gaps?\n- What experiments would strengthen the paper?\n\nOutput your review in this format:\n\n```\n## R1 Review: Methods & Experiments\n\n### Summary\n[2-3 sentences]\n\n### Strengths\n[Bulleted list, 4-6 items]\n\n### Weaknesses\n[Bulleted list, 4-8 items, each with severity: Major/Minor]\n\n### Missing Experiments or Analysis\n[What's absent that should be present]\n\n### Questions for Authors\n[3-5 specific questions]\n\n### Detailed Comments\n[Paragraph-form deeper analysis]\n\n### Preliminary Score: X/6\n### Preliminary Confidence: X/5\n```\n","uuid":"b8311e0e-8339-4366-b223-f5cb380c9f1a","session_id":"afaa0581-5224-4e41-930b-491fc2855128"}
