[x] Registry 清理：9 个过时 PREPARING 实验标记 killed ✅\\\\n- [x] paired-bootstrap 显著性检验（3 个 in-domain 比较 p<0.001）\\\\n- [x] analysis.tex 完成（§6.1-6.4: circular eval, TLM failure, error analysis, OB distant supervision）\\\\n- [ ] 🔴🔴 用户确认标注人力 → 启动 650 窗口标注\\\\n- [ ] f1-stag-analysis（已派 Agent，P1）— F1_stag per-class breakdown\\\\n- [ ] dream_simulate(review_mode=\\\\\\\"full\\\\\\\") — dream_20260514T214352 运行中\\\\n- [ ] paired-bootstrap 跨域修复（Worker 运行中）\\\\n- [ ] Paper Agent Full Draft（核心技术章节已完成，待 Intro/Related/Conclusion/Abstract）\\\\n- [ ] structural-data-scaling 结果论文呈现：必须在 circular eval caveat 框架下，不可表述为 data scarcity robustness\\\\n\\\\n## 关键路径时间线\\\\n```\\\\n5/14 NOW   论文数据错误修复完成 + analysis.tex 完成 + dream 运行中\\\\n5/14-16    Paper Agent Full Draft（不依赖 gold set 的章节）+ f1-stag-analysis\\\\n5/16       🔴 标注必须启动（最晚日期）\\\\n5/16-18    标注进行中 | 并行: 论文迭代\\\\n5/18-19    标注完成 → gold set 验证实验（pipeline 已就绪，一条命令出结果）\\\\n5/19-23    Paper Agent 补 gold set 结果 + 论文迭代 + polish\\\\n5/24-25    最终检查 + 提交\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## GPU 预算\\\\n- bjb2-23165: RTX 5090 32G × 2（cuda:0 + cuda:1）\\\\n- 当前：f1-stag-analysis 已派 Agent（待启动）; paired-bootstrap 跨域修复 Worker 运行中(CPU)\\\\n- 预估剩余 GPU 需求: ~2-4 GPU-hrs（f1-stag-analysis + gold set 验证）\\\\n\\\\n## 关键决策日志\\\\n\\\\n| ID | 日期 | 摘要 | 关联实验 |\\\\n|----|------|------|----------|\\\\n| D048 | 2026-05-14 | OH 权威标签源定为 windows_labeled.jsonl（20.87% stag），旧 em | cross-agent-structural, oh-full-finetune, oh-cmdrep-ablation, cross-agent-eval |\\\\n| D047 | 2026-05-14 | 暂停所有 OH 跨域数字引用，启动标签版本修复 | cross-agent-structural, oh-full-finetune, cross-agent-eval, oh-cmdrep-ablation |\\\\n| D046 | 2026-05-14 | 修正 cmd_rep ablation 数字 +21.6pp → +17.6pp，paper_fra | oh-cmdrep-ablation, cross-agent-structural |\\\\n| D045 | 2026-05-14 | BGE-M3 论文呈现：E5-large 为主力 encoder-agnostic 证据，BGE-M | encoder-e5, encoder-bge |\\\\n| D044 | 2026-05-14 | BGE-M3 multiseed 论文呈现：全报 mean±std，E5 做主力 encoder-a | encoder-e5, encoder-bge, probe-multiseed |\\\\n| D043 | 2026-05-14 | 冻结跨域结构特征数字（GB 0.967, +21.6pp），启动数据管道一致性调查 | cross-agent-structural, bootstrap-crossdomain-fix |\\\\n| D042 | 2026-05-14 | Baseline 数值引用规则：跨域 claim 统一用 cross-agent-structura | cross-agent-structural, structural-on-twv, non-nlp-baseline |\\\\n| D041 | 2026-05-14 | 写入 experiment_plan.yaml (32 experiments) + 更新 pape | oh-cmdrep-ablation, data-scaling-v2, ablation-window-size, oh-full-finetune |\\\\n| D040 | 2026-05-14 | D039 \\\\\\\"TLM 判死\\\\\\\" 结论暂缓：Reviewer 发现 σ=2.0 关键诊断未运行 + cro | temporal-label-model, twv-ablation, structural_on_twv |\\\\n| D039 | 2026-05-14 | TLM 彻底判死：structural-on-twv 证明 TWV 标签劣化下游分类器（最高 -21 | structural-on-twv, twv-ablation, temporal-label-model, cross-agent-structural |\\\\n\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 4032, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GdobHcVcqGQon44cqpBPfF","session_id":"afaa0581-5224-4e41-930b-491fc2855128","uuid":"3a3f81b4-9551-4f8b-b8d8-09e299cdea6b","timestamp":"2026-05-14T22:30:08.195Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XqDXiScXvhGaqp4Na6uxiv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N7EgbKWRQihTMUsrWaVab2","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R2 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept).\n\nYour focus areas: **Novelty**, **Related Work**, and **Presentation/Writing**.\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"Circular Evaluation as Systematic Risk in Weak Supervision for Sequential Agent Data\"\n8 pages, anonymous, dated May 14 2026.\n\nThe paper studies progress stagnation detection in LLM coding agents using weak supervision (labeling functions). The core finding: standard LF-derived evaluation massively overstates detector performance due to \"circular evaluation\"—training and evaluating on labels derived from features that overlap with classifier inputs. They construct a 650-window human-annotated gold set and show:\n\n1. **Inflation**: Structural classifiers drop from F1=0.995 to 0.74-0.76 on gold (25.5pp inflation); probes drop 15.5pp; LLM-as-judge *improves* by 6.8pp on gold.\n2. **Hierarchy collapse**: Structural-over-probe gap reverses from +9pp to -1pp; structural-over-LLM collapses from +24.3pp to +3pp. All methods converge to 0.73-0.77 band.\n3. **Temporal dynamics validated**: LF temporal roles (cmd_rep leading, outcome_bp lagging) preserved on gold (KW p=0.003).\n4. **Temporal label models fail**: TWV, HMM, lag-aware HMM all fail to beat majority vote.\n\nContributions claimed: (1) first quantification of circular eval inflation in weak supervision for sequential agent data (mean 21.5pp); (2) 650-window gold benchmark with IAA κ=0.72; (3) temporal dynamics are genuine but agent-specific; (4) negative result on temporal label models.\n\n## Paper Structure (8 pages)\n1. Introduction (p1-2): Motivates circular evaluation problem, lists 4 findings\n2. Related Work (p2): Three short paragraphs — Agent Monitoring, Weak Supervision/Data Programming, LLM-as-Judge\n3. Task and Data (p2-3): Problem formulation, 3 LFs described, agent trajectories (SWE-Agent, OpenHands), gold annotation (Table 1)\n4. Methods (p3): Four method families described briefly\n5. Experiments (p3-7): Sections 5.1-5.11 covering all major results\n6. Discussion (p7): Three discussion points\n7. Limitations (p7): One paragraph\n8. Conclusion (p8): One paragraph\n\n## Key Tables\n- Table 1: Gold set stats\n- Table 2: LF-Human confusion matrix\n- Table 3: Per-LF agreement\n- Table 4: Inflation/deflation summary (central result)\n- Table 5: Pairwise gap collapse\n- Table 6: Structural classifiers on gold (per-class)\n- Table 7: Probe performance across encoders\n- Table 8: Cross-agent evaluation\n- Table 9: F1_stag breakdown\n- Table 10: Error distribution\n- Table 11: Temporal dynamics\n\n**NOTE: The paper has NO figures at all — only tables.** The experiment plan described many figures (Sankey diagram, heatmaps, scatter plots, Venn diagram, dumbbell plot, radar chart, waterfall chart, etc.) but none appear in the paper.\n\n## Related Work Coverage in Paper\nThe paper's Related Work section (Section 2) is very brief (~3 short paragraphs):\n- **Agent Monitoring**: Mentions SlopCodeBench, CDCS, SpecRA, TrajAD, AgentPRM, Reflexion, LATS\n- **Weak Supervision**: Mentions Snorkel paradigm, conditional independence assumption\n- **LLM-as-Judge**: One sentence noting general trend + their baseline\n\n## Key Claims to Assess for Novelty\n1. \"First quantification of circular evaluation inflation in weak supervision for sequential data\" — Is this truly novel? Circular evaluation / label leakage is a known concern in ML.\n2. \"First human-annotated benchmark for agent stagnation\" — Novel resource contribution\n3. \"LF temporal dynamics are genuine but agent-specific\" — How novel vs incremental?\n4. \"Negative result on temporal label models\" — Value of negative results\n\n## Missing References to Check\n- The paper has broken citations: \"??\" appears in the introduction (page 1)\n- No reference list is included in the 8-page paper\n- Snorkel (Ratner et al.) is mentioned but not cited with a number\n- SlopCodeBench, CDCS, SpecRA, TrajAD, AgentPRM, Reflexion, LATS are mentioned by name but without proper citations\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate the following dimensions thoroughly:\n\n### 1. Novelty & Contribution\n- Is \"circular evaluation in weak supervision for sequential data\" a genuinely new insight?\n- How does this relate to known problems: label leakage, train-test contamination, Goodhart's law in evaluation?\n- Is the contribution primarily empirical (showing something happens) or methodological (solving it)?\n- Is the gold benchmark a meaningful contribution?\n- Is the negative result (TLMs fail) valuable?\n\n### 2. Related Work Coverage\n- Are key relevant works cited? Missing citations?\n- Is positioning against data programming literature adequate?\n- Are the broken citations (\"??\") a serious issue?\n- Is the comparison to existing agent monitoring work sufficient?\n\n### 3. Presentation & Writing Quality\n- Paper structure and flow\n- The complete absence of figures — how severe is this?\n- Clarity of the \"circular evaluation\" explanation\n- Are claims appropriately hedged?\n- Is the paper appropriately scoped for a top venue?\n\n### 4. Significance & Impact\n- Who would benefit from these findings?\n- Would this change practice in the field?\n- Is this a cautionary tale or does it advance the state of the art?\n\nOutput your review in this format:\n\n```\n## R2 Review: Novelty & Related Work\n\n### Summary\n[2-3 sentences]\n\n### Strengths\n[Bulleted list, 4-6 items]\n\n### Weaknesses\n[Bulleted list, 4-8 items, each with severity: Major/Minor]\n\n### Novelty Assessment\n[Detailed paragraph on novelty]\n\n### Related Work Gaps\n[What's missing from related work]\n\n### Presentation Issues\n[Specific issues with writing/figures/structure]\n\n### Questions for Authors\n[3-5 specific questions]\n\n### Detailed Comments\n[Paragraph-form deeper analysis]\n\n### Preliminary Score: X/6\n### Preliminary Confidence: X/5\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31144,"cache_read_input_tokens":22911,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31144},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afaa0581-5224-4e41-930b-491fc2855128","uuid":"fb972653-df5f-4cc2-9e21-6be746165c54"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"ac2b26c3beab028da","tool_use_id":"toolu_01N7EgbKWRQihTMUsrWaVab2","description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are Reviewer R2 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept).\n\nYour focus areas: **Novelty**, **Related Work**, and **Presentation/Writing**.\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"Circular Evaluation as Systematic Risk in Weak Supervision for Sequential Agent Data\"\n8 pages, anonymous, dated May 14 2026.\n\nThe paper studies progress stagnation detection in LLM coding agents using weak supervision (labeling functions). The core finding: standard LF-derived evaluation massively overstates detector performance due to \"circular evaluation\"—training and evaluating on labels derived from features that overlap with classifier inputs. They construct a 650-window human-annotated gold set and show:\n\n1. **Inflation**: Structural classifiers drop from F1=0.995 to 0.74-0.76 on gold (25.5pp inflation); probes drop 15.5pp; LLM-as-judge *improves* by 6.8pp on gold.\n2. **Hierarchy collapse**: Structural-over-probe gap reverses from +9pp to -1pp; structural-over-LLM collapses from +24.3pp to +3pp. All methods converge to 0.73-0.77 band.\n3. **Temporal dynamics validated**: LF temporal roles (cmd_rep leading, outcome_bp lagging) preserved on gold (KW p=0.003).\n4. **Temporal label models fail**: TWV, HMM, lag-aware HMM all fail to beat majority vote.\n\nContributions claimed: (1) first quantification of circular eval inflation in weak supervision for sequential agent data (mean 21.5pp); (2) 650-window gold benchmark with IAA κ=0.72; (3) temporal dynamics are genuine but agent-specific; (4) negative result on temporal label models.\n\n## Paper Structure (8 pages)\n1. Introduction (p1-2): Motivates circular evaluation problem, lists 4 findings\n2. Related Work (p2): Three short paragraphs — Agent Monitoring, Weak Supervision/Data Programming, LLM-as-Judge\n3. Task and Data (p2-3): Problem formulation, 3 LFs described, agent trajectories (SWE-Agent, OpenHands), gold annotation (Table 1)\n4. Methods (p3): Four method families described briefly\n5. Experiments (p3-7): Sections 5.1-5.11 covering all major results\n6. Discussion (p7): Three discussion points\n7. Limitations (p7): One paragraph\n8. Conclusion (p8): One paragraph\n\n## Key Tables\n- Table 1: Gold set stats\n- Table 2: LF-Human confusion matrix\n- Table 3: Per-LF agreement\n- Table 4: Inflation/deflation summary (central result)\n- Table 5: Pairwise gap collapse\n- Table 6: Structural classifiers on gold (per-class)\n- Table 7: Probe performance across encoders\n- Table 8: Cross-agent evaluation\n- Table 9: F1_stag breakdown\n- Table 10: Error distribution\n- Table 11: Temporal dynamics\n\n**NOTE: The paper has NO figures at all — only tables.** The experiment plan described many figures (Sankey diagram, heatmaps, scatter plots, Venn diagram, dumbbell plot, radar chart, waterfall chart, etc.) but none appear in the paper.\n\n## Related Work Coverage in Paper\nThe paper's Related Work section (Section 2) is very brief (~3 short paragraphs):\n- **Agent Monitoring**: Mentions SlopCodeBench, CDCS, SpecRA, TrajAD, AgentPRM, Reflexion, LATS\n- **Weak Supervision**: Mentions Snorkel paradigm, conditional independence assumption\n- **LLM-as-Judge**: One sentence noting general trend + their baseline\n\n## Key Claims to Assess for Novelty\n1. \"First quantification of circular evaluation inflation in weak supervision for sequential data\" — Is this truly novel? Circular evaluation / label leakage is a known concern in ML.\n2. \"First human-annotated benchmark for agent stagnation\" — Novel resource contribution\n3. \"LF temporal dynamics are genuine but agent-specific\" — How novel vs incremental?\n4. \"Negative result on temporal label models\" — Value of negative results\n\n## Missing References to Check\n- The paper has broken citations: \"??\" appears in the introduction (page 1)\n- No reference list is included in the 8-page paper\n- Snorkel (Ratner et al.) is mentioned but not cited with a number\n- SlopCodeBench, CDCS, SpecRA, TrajAD, AgentPRM, Reflexion, LATS are mentioned by name but without proper citations\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate the following dimensions thoroughly:\n\n### 1. Novelty & Contribution\n- Is \"circular evaluation in weak supervision for sequential data\" a genuinely new insight?\n- How does this relate to known problems: label leakage, train-test contamination, Goodhart's law in evaluation?\n- Is the contribution primarily empirical (showing something happens) or methodological (solving it)?\n- Is the gold benchmark a meaningful contribution?\n- Is the negative result (TLMs fail) valuable?\n\n### 2. Related Work Coverage\n- Are key relevant works cited? Missing citations?\n- Is positioning against data programming literature adequate?\n- Are the broken citations (\"??\") a serious issue?\n- Is the comparison to existing agent monitoring work sufficient?\n\n### 3. Presentation & Writing Quality\n- Paper structure and flow\n- The complete absence of figures — how severe is this?\n- Clarity of the \"circular evaluation\" explanation\n- Are claims appropriately hedged?\n- Is the paper appropriately scoped for a top venue?\n\n### 4. Significance & Impact\n- Who would benefit from these findings?\n- Would this change practice in the field?\n- Is this a cautionary tale or does it advance the state of the art?\n\nOutput your review in this format:\n\n```\n## R2 Review: Novelty & Related Work\n\n### Summary\n[2-3 sentences]\n\n### Strengths\n[Bulleted list, 4-6 items]\n\n### Weaknesses\n[Bulleted list, 4-8 items, each with severity: Major/Minor]\n\n### Novelty Assessment\n[Detailed paragraph on novelty]\n\n### Related Work Gaps\n[What's missing from related work]\n\n### Presentation Issues\n[Specific issues with writing/figures/structure]\n\n### Questions for Authors\n[3-5 specific questions]\n\n### Detailed Comments\n[Paragraph-form deeper analysis]\n\n### Preliminary Score: X/6\n### Preliminary Confidence: X/5\n```\n","uuid":"e33aabc1-4b07-4aba-8f9c-d226c9c27501","session_id":"afaa0581-5224-4e41-930b-491fc2855128"}
