{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018jQVryu2HmQunJD9Jtdtmy","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/paper/main.tex:21:\\newcommand{\\goldset}[1]{\\textcolor{blue}{[GOLD\\_SET: #1]}}\ndocs/paper/sections/analysis.tex:14:Second, a human-annotated gold set (\\S\\ref{sec:gold_set}) will provide definitive non-circular ground truth.\ndocs/paper/sections/experiments.tex:11:A human-annotated gold set provides the definitive non-circular evaluation (\\S\\ref{sec:gold_set}).\ndocs/paper/sections/experiments.tex:229:\\subsection{Gold Set Validation}\ndocs/paper/sections/experiments.tex:230:\\label{sec:gold_set}\ndocs/paper/sections/experiments.tex:231:\\goldset{Human-annotated gold set (650 windows) validation pending. Results will be added upon completion (expected 2026-05-17). This provides the non-circular ground truth evaluation for all methods.}\ndocs/paper/sections/conclusion.tex:24:Most critically, evaluation against human-annotated ground truth---for which we have prepared a 650-window gold set with a validated annotation pipeline---will determine whether structural features detect \\emph{real} stagnation or merely reconstruct labeling function outputs.\ndocs/paper/sections/limitations.tex:8:Cross-agent transfer (0.967) partially breaks this circularity, and we have prepared a 650-window gold set with a validated annotation pipeline; however, human annotation is pending, and all in-domain structural results should be interpreted with this caveat.\ndocs/paper/sections/introduction.tex:30:We note that in-domain evaluation uses silver labels (\\S\\ref{sec:circular}); cross-agent transfer and a pending gold set (\\S\\ref{sec:gold_set}) provide non-circular validation."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GdobHcVcqGQon44cqpBPfF","session_id":"afaa0581-5224-4e41-930b-491fc2855128","uuid":"2f5f45b9-0e2a-4b5a-b0e5-dbd89b55a705","timestamp":"2026-05-14T22:30:26.275Z"}
